WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:13.710
On Friday, June 28th 2019, it was announced
that the European Commission had reached an

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:38.680
agreement with Mercosur to create the largest
Free Trade Agreement in its history.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:43.700
It has taken 20 long years to reach an agreement
that affects a population of almost 800 million

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.690
people and a quarter of the world's GDP.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:55.360
Now, Mercosur, one of the most protectionist
and closed economic blocs in the world has

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:22.010
a 
huge opportunity to make the economies of

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:51.080
its member countries prosper: the EU is a

00:01:51.080 --> 00:02:08.280
colossus 
that

00:02:08.280 --> 00:03:09.629
buys more 
than two trillion dollars from the rest of

00:03:09.629 --> 00:03:15.980
the world every year.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:49.549
Dollars

00:03:49.549 --> 00:03:55.980
it spends on all kinds of products.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:30.780
Brazil, Argentina, Uruguay and Paraguay

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:54.680
now

00:04:54.680 --> 00:06:01.960
have before them

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:45.780
the best opportunity they’ve had in

00:06:45.780 --> 00:07:21.480
decades

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:39.280
to overcome their economic problems.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:08:05.669
There’s only

00:08:05.669 --> 00:16:07.699
one condition: they will have to compete.

